 "observations": [
  "The page number «205» stands at the head of the page, centred, with a rule below it; at the right the number of the table, «Tab. 90», in bold sans serif, underlined. The page has no signature. The title (L01), «Aequatio casarum duodecim signo piscium», the equation of the twelve houses for the sign of Pisces, in bold, without sigla. The folios of the manuscripts stand at the right of the title in two lines, «C 89r, O 146r,» and «N 55v.», the letters raised; here as right margin notes beside L01 and L02.",
  "The table: as on pp. 194-204 (JP2 0226-0236), the degrees of the ascendant, «Gradus aequales ortus piscium», in four lines, and five pairs «Gr.», «Min.» under «Secundum Aries [et Taurus]», «Tertium Taurus [et Gemini]», «Quartum Gemini [et Cancer]», «Quintum Cancer» and «Sextum Leo», the last two without a second sign: the beginnings of the fifth and the sixth house stay in Cancer and Leo for every degree of the ascendant. Here each head is set from the top, one printed line to a line (L02-L05); the units in L06; the cells separated by our «|»; a head followed by empty cells spans their columns. The names of the signs into which the beginnings pass stand in lines of their own over their columns: «Gemini» (L33) over the third house, «Taurus» (L35) over the second and «Cancer» (L38) over the fourth, each at the row where the computation passes into that sign. A short stroke above the 24 of the fifth house in L07; not transcribed.",
  "L07-L39. The beginnings of the houses for the ascendant at 1° to 30° of Pisces, by the rule of p. 194 (JP2 0226). Checked with the obliquity 23° 35′ and the latitude 38° 40′: the degrees and minutes agree within 2′ in 89 of the 150 places and within 3′ in 118; from 9° to 28° (L15-L36) the second to the fifth house lag behind the computation, the fourth by 2.4′ to 5.0′, most at 22°-24°, the third by 2.2′ to 3.8′, the second and the fifth by 2′ to 3.5′. The fifth and the sixth house grow by 39′ to 42′ and 49′ to 51′ a degree, the computed steps 40′ or 41′ and 49′ to 51′. At 30° (L39), when the ascendant is the vernal point, the fourth house begins at 0° 0′ of Cancer, as the computation gives.",
  "Notes on the readings. Checked by the computation and the steps of the columns: the edition's readings are the nearer at 5° and 12° in the second house (notes a and b: C's 20 against O's 24, C's 37 against O's 57; 10° 20.2′, 16° 38.8′ computed), at 8° in the third (note d: O's 49 against C's 46; 16° 49.4′), at 29° in the fourth (note f: the 29 of O and N against C's 28 in the degrees; 29° 27.2′), at 13°, 15° and 30° in the fifth (notes g, h and i: O's 16 and 17 against C's 17 and 18 in the degrees, the edition's 53 against the 13 of O and N and C's 22; 16° 32.3′, 17° 52.6′, 27° 53.1′), and at 9°, 13° and 14° in the sixth (notes k, l and m: the 20 of O and N against C's 9, the edition's 38 and 27 against the 28 and 37 of C and O; 10° 21.4′, 13° 39.1′, 14° 28.6′). At 22° in the second house (note c) the edition's 22, for the 26 of C and O, keeps the steps of the column, 52′ and 52′, where 26 gives 56′ and 48′ (25° 23.7′ computed); at 22° in the third (note e) C's 38 keeps them, 41′ and 41′, where O's 37 gives 40′ and 42′, both in the stretch that lags; at 19° in the sixth (note n) the 34 of C and O keeps them, 50′ and 50′, where the 38 added in the margin of O, nearer to the computation, 18° 36.5′, gives 54′ and 46′.",
  "Italics: «marg. adiec.»."
 ],
